    "dailyNotes": "### Handwritten Lecture Notes Summary (`Source_Files/Untitled Notebook(1).pdf` — Session 6)\n- **Jejunum vs. Ileum**:\n  - **Jejunum**: LUQ, taller/tighter plicae circulares, 1–2 arterial arcades, **long vasa recta**, less fat.\n  - **Ileum**: RLQ, fewer plicae, **more layers of arcades (3–5)**, **shorter vasa recta**, thick fat, Peyer's patches.\n- **Mesentery Defect**: Can cause an **internal hernia**.\n- **Autonomic Innervation**: Parasympathetic (Vagus / Pelvic splanchnic S2–S4) **promotes peristalsis** and secretion; Sympathetic (T10–L2) inhibits peristalsis and constricts sphincters.\n- **Appendix**: Trace **taeniae coli** along cecum to find the appendix base; majority are **retrocecal**.\n- **IMV Drainage Pathway**: $\\text{IMV} \\rightarrow \\text{Splenic Vein} \\rightarrow (+\\text{SMV}) = \\text{Portal Vein} \\rightarrow \\text{Liver} \\rightarrow \\text{Hepatic Veins} \\rightarrow \\text{IVC} \\rightarrow \\text{Heart}$.\n- **Dentate Line Rule**: Above = Internal Iliac / IMA nodes & Portal vein; Below = **Superficial Inguinal lymph nodes** & Caval (IVC) system (**changes cancer staging!**).",
