    "dailyNotes": "### Lecture & Handwritten Notes (`Source_Files/Histo .pdf` — Session 7)\n- **TEM Ultrastructure Rule (Handwritten on Slide 11)**:\n  - **Enteroendocrine (APUD) cell**: Small granules are in the **lower (basal) part of the cell** below the nucleus $\\rightarrow$ hormones diffuse into blood capillaries in the lamina propria.\n  - **Paneth cell**: Pyramid-shaped at crypt base; large eosinophilic granules in the **apical** cytoplasm $\\rightarrow$ secrete antimicrobial peptides (lysozyme, $\\alpha$-defensins) into the lumen to regulate the microbiome and protect adjacent Intestinal Stem Cells (ISCs).\n- **Tuft Cells (~0.4% of epithelium)**: Chemosensory cells with an apical tuft of rigid microvilli; detect intestinal helminths/parasites and secrete **IL-25** $\\rightarrow$ activates ILC2s (IL-13) $\\rightarrow$ goblet cell hyperplasia and mucin hypersecretion ('weep and sweep' worm expulsion within 7 days).\n- **Secretory IgA (sIgA) Transport**:\n  - Dimeric IgA (dIgA + J chain) from lamina propria plasma cells binds basolateral **pIgR** on enterocytes $\\rightarrow$ transcytosis $\\rightarrow$ released at brush border as **sIgA** wrapped in **secretory component (SC)**. Excess dIgA enters portal blood and is transported by hepatocytes into **bile**!\n- **Malabsorption Classification (Slide 26)**:\n  1. *Luminal phase*: Pancreatic enzyme or bile salt deficiency (fat/fat-soluble vitamin malabsorption).\n  2. *Brush-border phase*: Disaccharidase (lactase) deficiency (osmotic diarrhea).\n  3. *Mucosal/Enterocyte phase*: **Celiac sprue** (gluten/gliadin T-cell autoimmune enteropathy $\\rightarrow$ villous atrophy & crypt hyperplasia) or Crohn's disease.",
