        "stem": "A 58-year-old man with alcoholic cirrhosis presents with tense ascites, fever (38.4°C), and diffuse abdominal tenderness. Diagnostic paracentesis yields straw-colored fluid with Ascitic fluid albumin 0.7 g/dL, Serum albumin 3.1 g/dL, Ascitic total protein 1.1 g/dL, and Ascitic neutrophil (PMN) count 420 cells/mm³ (normal: <250 cells/mm³). What is the calculated Serum-Ascites Albumin Gradient (SAAG), its hemodynamic meaning, and the required antibiotic therapy?",
