        "stem": "During a hands-on point-of-care abdominal ultrasound session, a 42-year-old woman with postprandial right upper quadrant biliary colic is scanned in the supine and left lateral decubitus positions. Within the gallbladder lumen, the probe detects a highly echogenic focus that shifts to the dependent wall with posture change and casts a sharp, dark anechoic wedge directly behind it. Which acoustic physical property produces this dark posterior shadow?",
        "options": [
          "Refraction of sound waves across the smooth gallbladder muscularis",
          "Accelerated sound wave transmission through low-attenuation bile fluid",
          "Doppler frequency shift from turbulent blood flow in the cystic artery",
          "Reverberation artifacts between cholesterol crystals and intracellular gas",
          "Near-complete reflection and attenuation of the ultrasound beam by a dense gallstone"
        ],
