        "explanation": "Gallstones (cholelithiasis) appear on ultrasonography as mobile, dependent hyperechoic (bright) intraluminal structures accompanied by 'clean' posterior acoustic shadowing because the dense calcium/cholesterol matrix reflects and absorbs nearly all incident sound energy. In contrast, gallbladder polyps are non-mobile, do not cast a posterior acoustic shadow, and remain fixed to the wall."
