        "stem": "A 63-year-old man with Child-Pugh A hepatitis B cirrhosis has an unresectable 4.2-cm hypervascular hepatocellular carcinoma in Segment VIII of the liver, without main portal vein thrombosis or extrahepatic metastasis. He is referred to Interventional Radiology for Transarterial Chemoembolization (TACE), in which doxorubicin-eluting beads are infused selectively into the right hepatic arterial branch supplying the tumor. Why does embolizing the hepatic arterial branch selectively necrotize the tumor while sparing the surrounding normal liver parenchyma?",
