          "Normal hepatocytes rapidly catabolize doxorubicin via canalicular UGT1A1 glucuronidation",
          "Tumor neovessels lack endothelial tight junctions and trap large microspheres in the hepatic veins",
          "The caudate lobe provides retrograde arterial collateral flow exclusively to non-neoplastic hepatocytes",
          "Hepatocellular carcinomas derive ~90% of their blood supply from the hepatic artery, whereas normal parenchyma receives ~75% from the portal vein",
